 10`, `end_seconds: 20`)","id":"AC-1","seam":"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation (YouTube invalid-URL fallback)","then":"the returned string contains `> \"Relevant text\"` on its own line — the quoted transcript snippet is no longer dropped by the invalid-URL fallback","when":"`formatCitation(citation)` is called (exported from app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts)"},{"given":"the same citation as AC-1 (`video_url: 'not-a-url'`, `snippet: 'Relevant text'`)","id":"AC-2","seam":"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation (YouTube invalid-URL fallback)","then":"the returned string starts with `- ` and still contains `(timestamp link unavailable)` and `0:10–0:20`; the existing `console.warn` with exactly `[exportMarkdown] Skipping timestamp link — invalid video_url: \"not-a-url\"` still fires","when":"`formatCitation(citation)` is called"},{"given":"a citation with `source_type: 'dynamous'` and an empty `lesson_url` (e.g. `lesson_url: ''`), with a non-empty snippet (e.g. `Test snippet text`)","id":"AC-3","seam":"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation (Dynamous empty-lesson_url fallback)","then":"the returned string starts with `- `, contains no `](`, and still contains its snippet blockquote `> \"Test snippet text\"`","when":"`formatCitation(citation)` is called"},{"given":"a YouTube citation whose `video_url` parses but has no `v` parameter (e.g. `https://www.youtube.com/`) with a non-empty snippet","id":"AC-4","seam":"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation (YouTube missing-v-param fallback)","then":"the returned string starts with `- `, contains `(timestamp link unavailable)` and the `0:10–0:20` range, contains no markdown link to the title, and contains the quoted snippet blockquote — the no-`v`-param fallback is fixed identically to AC-1/AC-2","when":"`formatCitation(citation)` is called"},{"given":"a rendered sources list where one entry takes a fallback path (invalid URL or empty Dynamous lesson_url) and another entry takes a success path","id":"AC-5","seam":"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatSources (joined via formatCitation entries)","then":"every entry, including the fallbacks, begins with `- ` so each renders as its own markdown list item and no entry merges into the previous line","when":"`formatSources(citations)` assembles the export block"}],"dependencies":[],"invariants":["formatCitation continues to return '' for an empty, whitespace-only, or undefined snippet (the guard at the top of the function) — the fallback fix must not emit a bare `- ` line for snippetless citations.","The valid-URL YouTube path keeps its exact shape: `- [title](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=<id>&t=<start>s) — <range>\\n  > \"<snippet>\"` (existing tests assert the deep link and range).","The valid-lesson_url Dynamous path keeps its exact shape: `- [title](<lesson_url>) — <range>\\n  > \"<snippet>\"`.","Both YouTube fallbacks keep emitting `(timestamp link unavailable)` and the `<start>–<end>` range (en dash, produced by formatTimestamp), and keep calling console.warn with exactly `[exportMarkdown] Skipping timestamp link — invalid video_url: \"<video_url>\"` (existing test asserts the message with toHaveBeenCalledWith).","The Dynamous empty-lesson_url fallback keeps emitting no `](` anywhere in its output (existing test asserts not.toContain('](')).","formatTimestamp, the export header (`# <title>` + ISO date + `---`), the `**Sources:**` header, and the filename slug `conversation-<slug>-<date>.md` are unchanged.","Only two files change: production code in app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts and tests in the existing app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts; every current test case in that file must keep passing.","No new or version-changed packages: app/frontend/package.json and any lockfile are untouched, so no `## Dependency justification` section is needed.","No backend, schema, .env, CitationModal.tsx, Message.tsx, ChatArea.tsx, Sidebar.tsx, or src/lib/api.ts changes; api.ts types already make the AC fixtures type-check."],"issue":{"number":49,"title":"fix(export): markdown export drops the transcript snippet when a citation URL cannot be parsed"},"out_of_scope":["Backend, database schema, and any dependency or lockfile change.","CitationModal.tsx, Message.tsx, ChatArea.tsx, Sidebar.tsx, and src/lib/api.ts (types are sufficient as-is).","The valid-URL YouTube path and the valid-lesson_url Dynamous path — their output shape must not change.","formatTimestamp behaviour, the export header, and the filename slug.","Collapsing the duplicated console.warn blocks in the two YouTube fallback branches — pure refactor, not part of this bug.","Any .env file or deploy/ surface; nothing here needs a production secret or a manual smoke-test."],"risks":["Repro is DEFERRED TO RED: no existing command fails on the unchanged tree, so the red loop closes only when the new AC-1..AC-3 tests are added to app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts and proven failing there first; the deferred expected_symptom is `> \"Relevant text\"`. The AC-1 test should use a value-printing matcher (e.g. expect(result).toContain('> \"Relevant text\"')) consistent with the file's existing toContain style, so a red run actually prints that substring; if a boolean-wrapper assertion (expect(result.startsWith('- ')).toBe(true)) is used instead, the promised symptom may not appear in the red output.","The existing invalid-URL test (exportMarkdown.test.ts ~lines 215-227) asserts the console.warn message verbatim plus title presence, no markdown link, '(timestamp link unavailable)' and the range; the fix must satisfy those while adding the marker and snippet, or the suite regresses even as the new tests pass.","There are three separate fallback return statements (Dynamous empty lesson_url, YouTube invalid URL, YouTube missing v param). Fixing only some of them leaves the merge symptom alive on the uncovered path; AC-3/AC-4/AC-5 exist to force all three.","formatSources joins entries with a bare '\\n', so the fix's correctness depends entirely on each entry self-carrying the '- ' marker; the first entry must also keep rendering cleanly after the '**Sources:**' header line."],"summary":"In `formatCitation` (app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts), repair the three fallback returns so every emitted citation entry carries the `- ` list marker and preserves the quoted transcript snippet: the two YouTube fallbacks (unparseable `video_url`, and parseable URL with no `v` param) must append a `\\n  > \"<snippet>\"` blockquote line after the `title (timestamp link unavailable) — range` text, and the Dynamous empty-`lesson_url` fallback must be prefixed with `- `. This restores MISSION's every-cited-chunk-shows-its-snippet quality bar on the export path and stops fallback entries merging into the previous markdown list item (formatSources joins entries with a bare newline, so only the `- ` marker keeps each entry on its own list line).","version":"2.0"},"sha256":"0f0f2b9da5ee8de8c9ece7b28466b5ea331bc011d0038089f94a2263589fba27","source":"task-contract.json"},"design":{"content":{"ac_mapping":{"AC-1":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"AC-2":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"AC-3":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"AC-4":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"AC-5":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatSources"]},"allowed_new_files":[],"context_sha256":"2af6c6337227e84650af5383535509a377cb99a0d09fc811bfbadbd2814d0e91","contract_sha256":"0f0f2b9da5ee8de8c9ece7b28466b5ea331bc011d0038089f94a2263589fba27","data_flows":["Citation -> formatCitation -> '' when snippet is empty/whitespace/undefined, otherwise '- ' + title (markdown link on success paths, plain text + '(timestamp link unavailable)' on YouTube fallbacks) + ' — ' + range + '\\n  > \"<snippet>\"'","Citation[] -> formatSources -> '\\n\\n**Sources:**\\n' + formatCitation entries jo